# The build context is the repository root, as in
# `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .`. The Dockerfile copies only
# rust-toolchain.toml, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and crates/, so everything else
# is dead weight in the context. The one that matters most is data/: nozzl run
# from here with the shipped config/nozzl.toml writes its archive and logs
# there, and they change constantly while it runs.
.git/
target/
data/
docs/
scripts/
*.tar.gz
**/*.md
